# Audit Scanner — Environment Variables

# Database (shared Postgres with the backend; raw asyncpg, read-only).
# When set, the worker reads asset/credential context and integration_configs
# from this DSN. When unset, the worker can still run from a YAML mission
# file (phase 1 nice-to-have) — see templates/missions/.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://hakuna:hakuna@postgres:5432/hakuna

# Celery (use a different Redis DB to avoid queue collision with the
# VM scanner — VM uses /1, audit uses /2).
CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://redis:6379/2
CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://redis:6379/2

# Streaming pub-sub (engine publishes per-iteration events to
# audit:run:{run_id}). Defaults to CELERY_BROKER_URL — same Redis is
# fine. Backend's SSE endpoint subscribes and forwards. Unset →
# NullPublisher (transcript still in Celery result, no live updates).
REDIS_PUBSUB_URL=

# Relay agent transport. Two modes:
#   websocket — broadcast through the backend's RelayBroker (legacy).
#   http      — direct HTTPS to a relay node's /exec endpoint (OSS default).
# When unset, defaults to "http" with HAKUNA_RELAY_URL.
RELAY_TRANSPORT=http
HAKUNA_RELAY_URL=https://relay.local:8443
HAKUNA_RELAY_TOKEN=
RELAY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120

# LLM provider — same priority chain as the VM scanner. The first
# configured provider wins. Air-gapped deployments can rely on Ollama
# only; the worker degrades gracefully when no provider is configured
# (status=skipped, no crash).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Ollama is read from integration_configs only — set is_enabled=true and
# base_url there.

# Default model + budget per audit run. CLI / API requests can override.
AUDIT_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
AUDIT_DEFAULT_MAX_STEPS=20
AUDIT_DEFAULT_WALLCLOCK_S=600

# Mission templates directory. Optional YAML mission files registered at
# startup are loaded from here. Custom missions live under custom/.
TEMPLATES_DIR=/app/templates
